      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَوَّارَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَارَةٌ</span>, in two places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and see also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُوَّارَةٌ</span>, in two places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَائِرَةٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  Also [or
perhaps ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُوَّارَةٌ</span></b> ] The <i>pieces of wood which the
water turns so as to make the mill turn with their
turning.</i> (Mgh.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  And <i>A pair of compasses.</i>
(T, K, * TA.)

